WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.530
- I asked him about his
first performance ever,

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.120
what do you remember about yours?

00:00:03.120 --> 00:00:05.820
- Ooh, so I started off
doing singing competitions,

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:06.653
as you know,
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:00:06.653 --> 00:00:08.970
- and the last time, we talked about,

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:09.810
it was fun,

00:00:09.810 --> 00:00:12.210
and then when I first did my first show,

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:15.240
at The NorVa in Virginia
Beach, where I'm from,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.680
that was a whole different ballgame.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:18.540
And I still did a cover at the time.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.373
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:19.373 --> 00:00:22.297
- I was probably 10 or 11, and I sang

00:00:22.297 --> 00:00:24.090
"I Wanna Dance With
Somebody" by Whitney Houston.

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:26.040
- I love that, that was your song.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:26.873
- Oh, yep,

00:00:26.873 --> 00:00:27.706
there I am.
- Yeah.

00:00:27.706 --> 00:00:28.920
(Ava and audience laugh)

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:29.753
- I love that though.

00:00:29.753 --> 00:00:31.440
That's such a big, fun song.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:32.550
Everybody loves that song.

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:33.600
- [Ava] Yes, it was my favorite.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:34.433
I mean,
- Smart.

00:00:34.433 --> 00:00:35.266
- who didn't love Whitney?

00:00:35.266 --> 00:00:36.099
Who doesn't love Whitney?

00:00:36.099 --> 00:00:37.080
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:38.516
And if you don't, you're dumb.

00:00:38.516 --> 00:00:39.349
(Ava and audience laughs)

00:00:39.349 --> 00:00:40.560
So, you have no ears.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:41.910
- Oh no, yeah, don't wanna talk to you

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:42.787
if you don't love Whitney.

00:00:42.787 --> 00:00:44.820
- Oh yeah, I was like, what,
how do you not like her voice?

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:46.800
I heard that when you were out doing shows

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.320
that young though, your grandma
used to pet sit for you,

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:50.153
- [Ava] Oh.

00:00:50.153 --> 00:00:51.690
- and maybe she wasn't the best at it.

00:00:51.690 --> 00:00:53.638
- This is a funny story actually.

00:00:53.638 --> 00:00:54.471
(Ava laughs)
- [Kelly] Isn't it?

00:00:54.471 --> 00:00:55.470
- A lot of stories.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:58.560
Every time my family and
I would go on vacation,

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.020
if it was like five days or
seven days, I would leave my,

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:04.290
I had birds, with her, my cockatiels.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.320
- Okay.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:09.150
- And every time I came back,
the birds would be gone,

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:10.050
and the cage would be open,

00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:10.972
- [Seal] Oops.

00:01:10.972 --> 00:01:11.805
- and my grandma would be like,

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.110
"I just let them out for some air."

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:13.943
(audience laughs)

00:01:13.943 --> 00:01:16.080
And I'm like, "But for the third time,

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.160
you let them out for some air."

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:18.900
So, every time I got back from vacation,

00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:20.430
I would keep getting new birds.

00:01:20.430 --> 00:01:23.296
And I think, I don't
think she liked birds.

00:01:23.296 --> 00:01:24.129
(Ava and audience laugh)

00:01:24.129 --> 00:01:25.800
- Or she just didn't like them caged.

00:01:25.800 --> 00:01:27.090
She was like, "They wanna go out."

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:27.960
She was like, "They wanna go."

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:28.793
I just love-

00:01:28.793 --> 00:01:29.626
- Maybe that's what it is.

00:01:29.626 --> 00:01:30.459
But she really was just like,

00:01:30.459 --> 00:01:32.250
"I let them breathe some good fresh air,

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:33.562
and they didn't come back."

00:01:33.562 --> 00:01:34.395
(Ava and audience laugh)

00:01:34.395 --> 00:01:36.240
- I think the most amazing part is,

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:38.388
you kept allowing her to watch them.

00:01:38.388 --> 00:01:39.600
(Kelly and audience laugh)
- I know, I know.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.300
I was so young, I stopped
getting them after.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.133
I was like,

00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:44.610
- [Kelly] But obviously, she's
not gonna do it this time.

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:45.690
Oh my God.
- Get them again after.

00:01:45.690 --> 00:01:47.130
- I love that it's not like a normal pet

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:47.963
that most people pick.

00:01:47.963 --> 00:01:48.960
I love that you pick birds.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.836
That's so, well you're a
songbird, that makes sense.

00:01:50.836 --> 00:01:51.669
(Ava laughs)

00:01:51.669 --> 00:01:54.150
But anything ever gone
horribly wrong on stage,

00:01:54.150 --> 00:01:55.260
when you were just like, "Hmm."

00:01:55.260 --> 00:01:56.520
- [Ava] So many things.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.080
- Me too.
- So many things.

00:01:58.080 --> 00:02:00.540
Almost every time there's something,

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:02.550
'cause you think it's
gonna go the way you plan,

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.990
but no, it doesn't.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:06.600
And I usually have something like a shoe,

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:08.940
probably like, it's kind
of like, I have to wear

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:11.100
multiple socks under
my boots, in my boots.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.810
So, they're really tight.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.220
- Because I feel like if
they're a little loose,

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:15.750
I'm gonna fall.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.640
- So I tripped once.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:21.120
One other time my bra
popped off and thank God,

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:23.520
thank God I had this sparkly top

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.040
over the sheer top, but it was sheer.

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.717
So, when it popped off I was like, "Whoa."

00:02:28.717 --> 00:02:30.000
(audience laughs)
I'm like, "Okay,

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:31.620
hello everybody."

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:34.350
So I'm just gonna stay like
this and no one's gonna know.

00:02:34.350 --> 00:02:37.950
- Remind me not to buy that
bra, that specific brand.

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.990
- You know, I thought it was cute, but-

00:02:39.990 --> 00:02:41.190
- It's different when you have kids.

00:02:41.190 --> 00:02:42.828
It's not cute.

00:02:42.828 --> 00:02:44.325
(Kelly and audience laugh)

00:02:44.325 --> 00:02:45.480
It's different.

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.370
I give life to kids.

00:02:47.370 --> 00:02:48.230
So what's your moment?

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:49.897
Do you ever have a moment
on stage where you're like,

00:02:49.897 --> 00:02:52.620
"Okay, that was not planned."

00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:55.290
- Well, I remember doing a show once,

00:02:55.290 --> 00:02:57.540
it was part of a festival in Rio.

00:02:57.540 --> 00:03:00.270
I think it was, was it
Hollywood Rock or Rock in Rio

00:03:00.270 --> 00:03:01.680
or something like that.
- Okay.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.380
- And I remember running onto the stage,

00:03:04.380 --> 00:03:07.110
and they had these bright floor lights,

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:10.680
and I tripped, literally
before I sang a single note,

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:13.500
I tripped over the stage,
fell flat over the light,

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.190
fell flat on my face, cut up all my leg,

00:03:17.190 --> 00:03:19.593
and then had to kind of finish the show,

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:22.650
had to sing for the next hour,

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:23.483
- [Kelly] Oh!
- or so.

00:03:23.483 --> 00:03:26.133
- Do you get up, and
address it or do you not?

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:30.780
- Well, back then, I can't, what did I do?

00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:33.780
I was a bit shaken, but
I just kind of continued.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.610
- [Kelly] Oh.
- And now I'd probably,

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.520
I'd take a moment and
make fun of myself and-

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:40.434
- That's 100% me, yeah.

00:03:40.434 --> 00:03:41.267
- [Seal] So I'd probably-

00:03:41.267 --> 00:03:43.335
- I can't not talk about
it, 'cause it's funny,

00:03:43.335 --> 00:03:45.130
(Ava laughs)
falling is funny.

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:46.560
- Exactly, it is funny.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:47.880
- It's like, "Didn't plan on that,"

00:03:47.880 --> 00:03:50.490
but just right on my face in
front of thousands of people.

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:51.630
It totally happened to me too.

00:03:51.630 --> 00:03:52.665
Except the microphone was like,

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:53.820
(Kelly warbling)

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:54.860
and like the, yeah,
(Seal laughs)

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:55.950
it was the full moment.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:56.783
- [Ava] You really never know.

00:03:56.783 --> 00:03:58.363
- God thinks that I can
handle a lot, emotionally.

00:03:58.363 --> 00:03:59.880
- Oh!
(Ava and Kelly laugh)

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.880
Yeah, I was like, "All right, not cool."

